The plate looks like a square side plate of about 24 cm. The pile covers roughly 8 cm by 9 cm and is about 2 cm high, but it is loosely packed in chunks, so I estimate about 60 g.

The pile is white, soft and chunky with a slightly glossy, moist surface. That fits scrambled or cooked egg white better than cheese crumbles. Egg white is about 55 kcal/100 g, while fresh mozzarella would be about 250. It has no yellow, and its texture is spongy and irregular rather than crumbly like feta. I'm going with egg white.

